'''Minas Velti''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] [[Jedi Master]] who wielded a [[Color|green]]-bladed [[lightsaber]]. In [[19 BBY]], toward the end of the [[Clone Wars]], she was [[Jedi training|training]] a [[Reva Sevander's Initiate clan|group]] of [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] at the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] when [[clone trooper]]s of the [[501st Legion]] stormed the [[Jedi temple|temple]] as part of [[Operation: Knightfall]]. Velti attempted to defend the [[youngling]]s but ultimately [[Death|perished]] during the siege.

==Biography==
{{Quote|What do we do now?''"<br />"''We run.|The younglings after Minas Velti's death|audio=WhatNow-PartI.flac|<ref name="Part I" />}}
[[File:MinasVeltiInAction-OWK1.png|thumb|left|300px|Minas Velti defended her students during the Siege of the Jedi Temple.]]
Minas Velti served the [[Jedi Order]]<ref name="Topps" /> and the [[Galactic Republic]]<ref name="ToppsRep" /> as a [[Jedi Master]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Topps" /> In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Kenobi 1" /> Velti led a [[Reva Sevander's Initiate clan|group]] of [[Jedi Initiate]]s&mdash;including [[Faris]] and [[Reva Sevander]]&mdash;<ref name="Part I" />through [[meditation]] [[Jedi training|exercises]]<ref name="SWE">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> on a balcony within the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on<ref name="Part I" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Coruscant]],<ref name="Part I" /> her [[homeworld]].<ref name="Topps" /> Carrying out [[Order 66]]<ref name="Part I" />&mdash;the [[Executive Order Codes for the Grand Army of the Republic|command]] for [[clone trooper]]s to [[Great Jedi Purge|eliminate]] the [[Jedi]]<ref name="USWNE" />&mdash;two [[trooper]]s of the [[501st Legion]] [[Operation: Knightfall|interrupted]] the training by opening fire on Velti and her [[Clan (Jedi)|students]]. Velti deflected the [[DC-15A blaster carbine|blaster]] bolts and [[Death|eliminated]] the troopers.<ref name="Part I" />

The Jedi Master ushered the [[youngling]]s through the [[Jedi temple|temple]] and continued to defend them from the ongoing siege. Despite cutting down multiple [[Cloning|clones]], Velti was soon overwhelmed as she brought the children to the main hall. Velti fell to a [[blaster]] bolt to her [[stomach]] as she killed the last clone immediately threatening the children. Afterward, the younglings grieved over her body before deciding they had to continue running;<ref name="Part I" /> however, they then encountered the fallen Jedi [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] and fell to his [[Skywalker lightsaber|lightsaber]], with only Sevander surviving.<ref name="Part V">{{Kenobi|Part V}}</ref> Later, clone troopers searched the Jedi Temple to catalog the Jedi that perished,<ref name="Master">''[[Master of Evil]]''</ref> which included Velti.<ref name="Part I" /> The fallen Jedi's lightsaber was collected along with the other abandoned sabers.<ref name="Master" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Uunh!|Minas Velti, dying|<ref name="Kenobi 1" />}}
[[File:MinasVeltiDies-OWKpI.png|thumb|right|300px|Velti died defending Jedi Initiates.]]
Minas Velti was a [[human]]<ref name="Topps" /> [[Gender|female]]<ref name="Women" /> with [[Color|black]] [[hair]], tan skin, and brown [[eye]]s. During the attack on the Jedi Temple, Velti valiantly<ref name="Topps" /> aided the attempted escape of her five students but was ultimately killed.<ref name="Part I" />

==Powers and abilities==
{{Quote|Come on! Move! Quick!|Minas Velti|<ref name="Part I" />}}
Velti was [[Force-sensitive]] and could [[Lightsaber combat|wield]] a lightsaber to deflect blaster bolts.<ref name="Part I" />

==Equipment==
Velti wielded a green-bladed lightsaber and wore brown [[Jedi apparel|Jedi robes]].<ref name="Part I" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I'm grateful to have chance to play Jedi master Minas Veiti ''[sic]'' on Obi Wan. Thank you Deborah for choose ''[sic]'' me, our awesome cast and crew, our stunt coordinator Jonathan Eusebio, my jedi younglings!|Ming Qiu on Instagram|<ref name="MingInsta">{{Instagram|username=sunmoonl|url=p/CfP4JErp1he|name=[[Ming Qiu]]|date=2022-06-26|quote=I'm grateful to have chance to play Jedi master Minas Veiti [''sic''] on Obi Wan. Thank you Deborah for choose [''sic''] me, our awesome cast and crew, our stunt coordinator Jonathan Eusebio, my jedi younglings! The photo is by Matt Kennedy|archiveurl=https://archive.is/qZUYK}}</ref>}}
Minas Velti first appeared in "[[Part I]]," the first episode of the television series ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'',<ref name="Part I" /> which premiered on [[May 26]], [[2022]].<ref name="Release">{{InsiderCite|214|Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi Companion|''Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi'' Companion}}</ref> While unnamed in the episode, the credits identified her as "Jedi Master Minas Velti," and she was portrayed by [[Ming Qiu]]. Director<ref name="Part I" /> [[Deborah Chow]] chose Qiu to play the character, for which Qiu expressed gratitude. On [[Wikipedia:Instagram|Instagram]], Qiu thanked Chow, stunt coordinator [[Jonathan (Jojo) Eusebio|Jonathan Eusebio]], the actors who played the Jedi younglings, and the cast and crew.<ref name="MingInsta" />

The [[2023 Topps Star Wars|2023 Topps ''Star Wars'']] collectible card set, which released on [[August 4]], [[2023]],<ref name="ToppsRelease">{{ToppsRipped|url=2023-topps-star-wars-checklist-spotlight|text=Checklist Spotlight: 2023 Topps Star Wars|quote=Release Date: August 4, 2023}}</ref> featured cards of individuals, including Velti, with their "homeworld" listed.<ref name="Topps" /> [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Pablo Hidalgo]] has described the set's use of the term as a "poor choice" of description for planets that the characters were merely associated with.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1693067125491912721|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2023-08-20|quote=It sounds like a poor choice of description of a planet they happen to be associated with.|archivedate=20230820012834}}</ref> This article, however, assumes that the information on Velti's card is still applicable.

